From 02cfdb879606eb8ce0edde365e3cea260f5221ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 16:18:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild owner side to actually match the approved mockup
 structure
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Previous batches recolored the existing owner components (FleetDriverCard,
InspectionFleetRow) instead of restructuring them, so the information
architecture stayed closer to the old fleet-management look even though the
palette changed. This rebuilds the three owner screens to the mockup's
actual layout:

- Home: simple driver list (avatar, name, vehicle + driving/parked, trust
  number) instead of the expandable-chip card, plus an aggregate
  needs-attention card and a "this week" fleet distance/payments stat pair.
- Inspection tab: an aggregate rental-health checklist across the fleet,
  and a plain vehicle list with health-score pills, instead of one detailed
  card per driver.
- Rental tab: now just a driver list (name, vehicle, since-date) that drills
  into a new dedicated profile screen — payment-term progress, TrustScore
  ring, a "what affects this score" checklist, and a profile block (phone,
  licence, rentals completed). This is also where "Manage Reference Photos"
  now lives for the owner, since that action had no clear home before.

New src/hooks/useOwnerFleetSummary.ts backs all three screens with a single
bulk query instead of duplicating per-row fetches. FleetDriverCard and
InspectionFleetRow are removed as dead code now that nothing renders them.
